# Frontend tooling & rules

The cross-tool source of truth for UI work is **`FRONTEND_TOOLING.md`** at the repo
root. Read it for anything touching the frontend. Summary:

## Installed packages (use them when available)
- **MCP servers** (`.mcp.json`): `shadcn` (add registry components), `chrome-devtools`
  (run + inspect + screenshot the change in a browser), `@21st-dev/magic` (generate
  net-new components, then adapt to our conventions).
- **Design skills** (`.claude/skills/`): `frontend-design` (aesthetic direction for new
  surfaces) and `web-design-guidelines` (accessibility / UX review).

## Hard rules
- This app is **shadcn/ui + Tailwind** (`components.json`). Prefer an existing shadcn
  component or `src/components/ui/*` primitive before hand-rolling one.
- **Semantic design tokens only** — never raw Tailwind palette classes (`bg-blue-500`,
  `text-red-600`) or hardcoded hex/font values in shared UI. Consume the white-label CSS
  tokens (`docs/WHITE_LABEL_TOKEN_CONTRACT.md`). `npm run audit:style` fails on new
  hardcoded-color/font violations (new = 0).
- Respect `components.json` aliases and the existing `tailwind.config.ts` / `src/index.css`.
- Accessibility floor: visible focus, correct semantics/labels, `prefers-reduced-motion`,
  responsive to mobile.
- Before finishing a UI change: `npm run lint`, `npm run audit:style`, `npm run build`.

Backend / security / AML rules: see `AGENTS.md` and `AGENTS_NPC_Property_Dashboard.md`.
